;; A Raspberry Pi 5 that captures from either camera and serves it.
;;
;; Open http://<board>/ and the landing page has the live stream, the
;; recordings and the commands. With no camera attached, every command
;; takes "test" and generates a pattern, so the image is worth flashing
;; before the hardware arrives.
;;
;; No hardware H.264 encoder on this board - Broadcom removed it for the
;; Pi 5 - so recording and RTP are software x264 on the CPU, and MJPEG is
;; the path that stays cheap. feature:media-kit's comment has the detail.
;;
;; The rootfs is larger than the board profile's default because GStreamer,
;; libcamera-apps (which brings boost), ffmpeg and lighttpd are not small,
;; and /var/www/rec fills with MP4 segments while recording.

(image raspberrypi5-media
  (compose
    image:raspberrypi5
    feature:dev-ssh
    feature:media-kit)

  (override
    (value buildroot:BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_EXT2_SIZE "2G"))

  (verified-against (buildroot "2025.02.16")))
